# Your two DGX Sparks. Copy this file to config/cluster.env and edit it:
#
#   cp config/cluster.env.example config/cluster.env
#
# Every DGX Spark recipe reads it. Run the recipes from Spark 1 (the head): it serves HTTP, and it reaches
# Spark 2 over SSH. ./tools/doctor.sh checks every value below.

# --- SSH -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How Spark 1 reaches Spark 2 over SSH (a host alias from ~/.ssh/config works). Must work without a password:
#   ssh-copy-id <user>@<spark2>      then      ssh -o BatchMode=yes <spark2> true
SPARK2_SSH=spark2

# --- The direct 200 Gb/s link (QSFP cable between the two ConnectX-7 ports) ----------------------------------
# The addresses each Spark has on that link. docs/01-hardware-setup.md shows how to set them.
SPARK1_LINK_IP=192.168.100.1
SPARK2_LINK_IP=192.168.100.2

# The link's network interface and RDMA adapter(s), from `ibdev2netdev` on Spark 1 (the "(Up)" lines).
# GB10 shows four adapters and two of them are down; pin the ones that are up, or NCCL may pick a dead one.
NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=enp1s0f1np1
NCCL_IB_HCA=rocep1s0f1,roceP2p1s0f1
# RoCE v2 over IPv4 usually sits at GID index 3 (check with show_gids). Leave empty to let NCCL choose.
NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=3

# --- Where things live (the same paths on both Sparks) --------------------------------------------------------
HF_CACHE=$HOME/.cache/huggingface          # model weights (Hugging Face cache layout)
KERNEL_CACHE=$HOME/.cache/tensorfold-kernels # compiled CUDA/Triton kernels, kept across container restarts

# --- Downloads -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How Spark 2 gets its copy of the weights:
#   pull  = both Sparks download from Hugging Face at the same time
#   rsync = Spark 1 downloads once, then copies over the 200 Gb/s link (much faster for 180-340 GB models)
WEIGHTS_SYNC=rsync
# HF_TOKEN=hf_...                           # only for gated or rate-limited downloads

# --- The API ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every recipe serves an OpenAI-compatible API on Spark 1 at http://<spark1>:$PORT/v1 (one model at a time).
PORT=8080
# The address you use from your laptop to reach Spark 1 (for benchmarks run from the Mac).
SPARK1_LAN=spark1.local
